the un inquiry accused the regime of kim  jong-un of widespread crimes against  humanity  the chairperson of the inquiry said they  were sanctioned at the highest level in  north korea  and called for the international  community to take action  contending with the scourges of nazism  apartheid the khmer rouge and other  affronts  required great courage by great nations  and by ordinary human beings alike  it is now your solemn duty to address  the scourge of human rights violations  and crimes against humanity in the  democratic people's republic of korea  but china dismissed the un report  because no information had been gathered  in north korea itself  the inability of the commission to get  support and cooperation from the country  concerned makes it impossible for the  commission to carry out its mandate in  an impartial objective and effective  manner  the eu has called for north korea to be  referred to the international criminal  court  but as a permanent member of the  security council china has the power to  veto any resolution against pyongyang
 

